@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents/deploy/prepare + /send — deploy agent code as a running contract
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Agent owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsApiSdk\n.deploy(id, version) |\n.deployCode(code)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "EmbersEvents\n(WebSocket)" as Events #E3D8F5
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6

group Phase 1 — prepare (deploys nothing)
SDK -> API : POST /api/ai-agents/deploy/prepare\n{ type: "Agent", id, version, address }\nor { type: "Code", code }
API -> Domain : prepare_deploy_contract
alt type = "Agent" — deploy a stored version
  Domain -> Chain : read the stored agent\n(retry 10 x 500 ms for observer lag)
  Chain --> Domain : Agent { code, ... }
  Domain -> Domain : reject when absent or empty:\n"agent not found" / "agent has no code"
  Domain -> Domain : render deploy_agent.rho —\nbind the entry contract to handle\n"agent:{id}:{version}"
  Domain -> Domain : render record_deploy.rho —\nthe system contract stamping\nlast_deploy on the stored record
  Domain --> API : DeployAgentResp\n{ contract, system }
else type = "Code" — deploy raw source
  Domain -> Domain : pass the source through verbatim
  Domain --> API : DeployAgentResp { contract }
end
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }
end

group Sign, subscribe, send
SDK -> SDK : signContract(contract, privateKey)
SDK -> SDK : signContract(system, privateKey)\nwhen present — same wallet key
SDK -> Events : subscribeForDeploy(\n  hex(contract.sig).toLowerCase(), maxWait)
SDK -> API : POST /api/ai-agents/deploy/send\n{ prepare_request, prepare_response,\n  request: { contract, system? }, token }
API -> API : verify the echo hash binding
API -> Domain : deploy_signed_deploy
Domain -> Chain : deploy MAIN contract
Chain --> Domain : main deploy id
alt system contract present (type = "Agent")
  Domain -> Chain : deploy SYSTEM contract
  Chain --> Domain : system deploy id
  API <-- Domain : system deploy id\n(the final ordered write)
else no system contract (type = "Code")
  API <-- Domain : main deploy id
end
SDK <-- API : 200 SendResp { deploy_id }
SDK --> Owner : { prepareResponse, sendResponse,\n  waitForFinalization }
end

group Finalization — observed on the WebSocket
Chain --> Events : Finalized { deploy_id: hex(contract.sig),\n  ..., node_type: Observer }
Events --> Owner : waitForFinalization resolves\n(keyed on the MAIN contract)
end

note over API #FFF6C9
For type "Agent", two identifiers exist: the
response's deploy_id names the SYSTEM write
(the synchronization barrier), while the SDK's
finalization wait is keyed on the MAIN
contract's signature. Both deploys finalize;
they are different deploys.
end note

note over Domain #FFF0C7
The stored code is deployed verbatim. An agent
authored for a team context is rejected: its
"main" is a free name at the top level of a
standalone deploy.
end note
@enduml
